# tests/base/clskit_range_top.rxt — [CLS-TREE] S2 (D139): the one range
# spelling's TOP BYTE, as ANSWERS.
#
# Since D139 a VM class read and a DFA scan edge spell a one-interval byte
# class through the same emitter (`pcrec_clskit_emit_inline`,
# `(unsigned)(byte - lo) <= span`). Every other corpus file's subjects stop
# short of a range's top byte (`\d` subjects never carry a 9, `[a-z]` ones
# never a z), so a span spelled one short (S434) read as UNDETECTED. Each
# subject below ENDS ITS RUN on the top byte of the class that extends it.
# Expectations are python3 re spans (re.search), transcribed unmodified.

# a capture-bearing pattern (VM): the run ends on z
pattern ([a-z]+)x
m "zzx" 0 3
g 1 0 2

# a scan-edge run on the DFA, both ends of a run on z
pattern [a-z]+@[a-z]+$
m "az@zz" 0 5

# digit runs ending on 9, captured (VM)
pattern (\d+)-(\d+)
m "99-99" 0 5
g 1 0 2
g 2 3 5

# digit run on the DFA, ending on 9
pattern [0-9]+z$
m "99z" 0 3
